  "notes": "{当|あ}てはめる means to apply or fit something (a rule, theory, formula) to a specific case or situation.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {当|あ}てはまる (intransitive — \"to apply to, to fit\")\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{当|あ}てはめている indicates someone is in the process of applying something.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {規則|きそく}を{当|あ}てはめる: to apply a rule\n- {公式|こうしき}を{当|あ}てはめる: to apply a formula\n- {理論|りろん}を{現実|げんじつ}に{当|あ}てはめる: to apply theory to reality\n- {基準|きじゅん}を{当|あ}てはめる: to apply a standard\n\nUSAGE:\nThe particle pattern is AをBに{当|あ}てはめる (apply A to B). The intransitive pair {当|あ}てはまる uses AがBに{当|あ}てはまる (A applies to B).",
